From: matthane <matthan.evans@icloud.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 07:51:58 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] DVDClock: take the clock lock when reading the absolute clock

GetClock(absolute) advances the speed adjust state and may restart the
clock mapping under the system lock only. GetClock() and every other
writer of that state hold the clock lock, so the two can interleave
and lose a step of the clock.
---
 xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDClock.cpp | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDClock.cpp b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDClock.cpp
--- a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDClock.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDClock.cpp
@@ -0,6 +0,7 @@
 
 double CDVDClock::GetClock(double& absolute, bool interpolated /*= true*/)
 {
+  std::unique_lock critLock(m_critSection);
   int64_t current = m_videoRefClock->GetTime(interpolated);
 
   std::unique_lock lock(m_systemsection);
